## Commands

Commands are messages from a client to a server.  A command is the mirror image of a signal: it travels client to server instead of server to client.  Put another way, it is a method call with no response.
Commands are fire-and-forget.  There is no response message, so a client never learns whether the server acted on the command, and the server never learns which client sent it.

```plantuml
@startuml
Client ->> Server : Command(Parameters)
@enduml
```
